      "text": "Let $\\mathbf{p}=(x,y)$ be the midpoint of the segment with endpoints\n$(-3,-4)$ and $(4,-5)$. Then by the midpoint formula, we have\n\\[\\mathbf{p}=\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{pmatrix}-3 \\\\ -4\\end{pmatrix}+\n\\begin{pmatrix}4 \\\\ -5\\end{pmatrix})=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ -9\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2}\\end{pmatrix}.\\]\nThe distance between any point $(x,y)$ and the midpoint $\\mathbf{p}$ is\n\\[\\sqrt{\\left(x-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2+}\\left(y+\\frac{9}{2}\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{\\left(x-0-\\frac{1}{2}-0\\right)^2+\\left(y+0-\\frac{9}{2}+0\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{x^2-2x+1+\\left(y+\\frac{9}{2}\\right)^2}.\\]Plugging in the coordinates of $(-3,-4)$ for $(x,y),$ we have\n\\[\\sqrt{(-3)^2-2(-3)+1+\\left(-4+\\frac{9}{2}\\right)^{2}}=\\sqrt{25+1+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{27+\\frac{1}{4}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{111}{4}}=\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{111}}{2}}.\\]The answer is: \\frac{\\sqrt{111}}{2}",
